'''Llanquihue''' (from {{Langx|arn|Llanquyn-we-laufken}}; {{Literal translation|to be hidden|to be lost|sunken place}}) is a [[W:Lake|lake]] on the island of [[Cerdanya|''Tinguiririca'']], wedged between [[Cerdanya]] and [[Hesperia]]. It is the largest freshwater lake in [[Balisca]] and the 13th largest in the world, with a surface area of {{convert|4524.99|km2|mi2|0|abbr=on}} and a maximum width of {{convert|98|mi|km|0|abbr=on}}. The lake's waters have an average depth of {{convert|158|m|ft|0|abbr=on}}, with a maximum depth of {{convert|623|m|ft|0|abbr=on}}. 

The deepest point of the lake is situated in the end of its narrow south-southwestern arm, in front of the retreating [[Rangkawe Glacier|''Rangkawe'' Glacier]]. The north-northeastern arm ends in front of the  [[Kafürwe Glacier|''Kafürwe'' Glacier]]. The glaciers debouch into the lake at these sites, making "trenches" in the bedrock.

